Chapter: RealSaturating
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 `Real saturating` clamps a result that leaves the finite range to the
 largest finite magnitude of the same sign, and answers zero for a NaN.

 This test used to add 3.0 and 4.0 and divide zero by zero, and that is all.
 Neither case leaves the finite range, so it exercised the arithmetic and
 never the mode: the emitter clamped nothing at all, and an overflow
 returned a plain infinity for as long as the mode has existed. A test that
 cannot reach the behaviour it names is the shape ExaminersAssay calls a
 function that always answers the same thing.

 The operands are built from bit patterns rather than written as decimals
 because the largest finite double has no short decimal form, and a literal
 close to it would test a different number than the one at the boundary.

 Answers are compared as bit patterns. The difference between the largest
 finite double and infinity is one in the last place of the exponent field,
 and every decimal rendering of the two that this compiler can produce looks
 identical.

Section: Operands

  real-max : Real
  real-max = bits-to-real #7FEFFFFFFFFFFFFF

  real-min : Real
  real-min = bits-to-real #FFEFFFFFFFFFFFFF

Section: Ops

  add-sat : Real saturating, Real saturating -> Real saturating
  add-sat (a) (b) = a + b

  sub-sat : Real saturating, Real saturating -> Real saturating
  sub-sat (a) (b) = a - b

  mul-sat : Real saturating, Real saturating -> Real saturating
  mul-sat (a) (b) = a * b

  div-sat : Real saturating, Real saturating -> Real saturating
  div-sat (a) (b) = a / b

  sat-bits : Real saturating -> Integer
  sat-bits (x) = real-to-bits (from-real-saturating x)

Section: Report

 Each line names what the mode must do. The finite cases are controls: a
 mode that clamped everything, or that had simply replaced arithmetic with a
 constant, would fail them.

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
    print-line-uni ("finite-add " & show (sat-bits (add-sat (to-real-saturating 3.0) (to-real-saturating 4.0))))
    print-line-uni ("finite-div " & show (sat-bits (div-sat (to-real-saturating 7.0) (to-real-saturating 2.0))))
    print-line-uni ("ovf-add " & show (sat-bits (add-sat (to-real-saturating real-max) (to-real-saturating real-max))))
    print-line-uni ("ovf-mul " & show (sat-bits (mul-sat (to-real-saturating real-max) (to-real-saturating 2.0))))
    print-line-uni ("ovf-neg " & show (sat-bits (add-sat (to-real-saturating real-min) (to-real-saturating real-min))))
    print-line-uni ("ovf-sub " & show (sat-bits (sub-sat (to-real-saturating real-min) (to-real-saturating real-max))))
    print-line-uni ("ovf-div " & show (sat-bits (div-sat (to-real-saturating real-max) (to-real-saturating 0.5))))
    print-line-uni ("nan-zero " & show (sat-bits (div-sat (to-real-saturating 0.0) (to-real-saturating 0.0))))
    print-line-uni ("nan-safe " & show (sat-bits (add-sat (div-sat (to-real-saturating 0.0) (to-real-saturating 0.0)) (to-real-saturating 1.0))))
  end
